<p id="A3.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">and the same bound applies to differences. Conditional expectation is
an <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction, and (<a href="#A2.E13" title="Equation B.13 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Uniform macroscopic coercivity). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.13</span></a>) controls the
left side. Thus every term in (<a href="#A3.E8" title="Equation C.8 ‣ Lemma C.1 (Derivative formula for 𝖴_𝖯𝖯). ‣ C.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix C Macroscopic coercivity and the half-turn bound ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.8</span></a>) is
continuous under <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> approximation. Density of
<math id="A3.SS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>c</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\rm c}^{\infty}(\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>Y</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\pi_{\eta}^{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>